  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q18-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Solve $\\log_3(t)-\\log_3(t^2-4)=-1$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$t=4$\n\nUse the quotient law to form a quadratic, then reject roots outside the original logarithm domain.",
      "worked": "The domain requires $t>0$ and $t^2-4>0$, so $t>2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_3\\left(\\frac{t}{t^2-4}\\right)&=-1\\\\\\frac{t}{t^2-4}&=3^{-1}\\\\\\frac{t}{t^2-4}&=\\frac13\\\\3t&=t^2-4\\\\t^2-3t-4&=0\\\\(t-4)(t+1)&=0\\\\t&=4\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$\nReject $t=-1$ because $\\log_3 t$ is undefined.\n\n$$t=4$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
